   <div class="col-lg-8">
         <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="TNEA 2026 Registration Start Date – Counselling &amp; Rank List Details">
         <div class="blog-content">
             <div class="blog-body">
                 <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">TNEA 2026: Decoding Registration, Counselling, and Rank List Details for Aspiring Engineers</h1>
                 <p class="lead">Aspiring engineers in Tamil Nadu, gear up! The Tamil Nadu Engineering Admissions (TNEA) 2026 is on the horizon, offering a streamlined pathway to undergraduate engineering programs across the state. This comprehensive guide provides you with the latest tentative information regarding registration dates, counselling procedures, and rank list details to help you navigate your admission journey with confidence.</p>

                 <p>TNEA is a single-window admission system conducted by the Directorate of Technical Education (DoTE), Chennai, on behalf of Anna University. Unlike many other states, TNEA admissions are based purely on Class 12 marks in Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics, making your academic performance crucial for securing a seat in your desired college and branch.</p>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">Key Highlights of TNEA 2026</h2>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ Admissions are based on Class 12 (PCM) marks, not an entrance exam.</p>
                   <p>✅ Conducted by DoTE, Chennai, for B.E./B.Tech courses across government, government-aided, university departments, and self-financing colleges.</p>
                   <p>✅ Entire application and counselling process is conducted online, with certificate verification at TNEA Facilitation Centres (TFCs).</p>
                   <p>✅ A unique random number is assigned to candidates to resolve tie-breaking situations in the rank list.</p>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">TNEA 2026 Tentative Important Dates</h2>
                 <p>While official announcements are typically released closer to the application period, based on previous trends and current information, here's a tentative schedule for TNEA 2026. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official TNEA website (tneaonline.org) for confirmed dates.</p>

                 <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                     <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                         <thead>
                             <tr>
                                 <th>Event</th>
                                 <th>Tentative Dates</th>
                             </tr>
                         </thead>
                         <tbody>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Official Notification Release</td>
                                 <td>April 2026</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Online Registration Start Date</td>
                                 <td>First week of May 2026 (e.g., May 6, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Last Date for Online Registration</td>
                                 <td>First week of June 2026 (e.g., June 5, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Last Date for Document Upload</td>
                                 <td>First week of June 2026 (e.g., June 8, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Certificate Verification</td>
                                 <td>June 10-20, 2026 (at TFCs)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Random Number Assignment</td>
                                 <td>June 2026 (e.g., June 11, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Rank List Publication</td>
                                 <td>End of June 2026 (e.g., June 27, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Grievance Redressal Period</td>
                                 <td>Late June - Early July 2026 (e.g., June 28 – July 2, 2026)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Counselling (Choice Filling &amp; Allotment)</td>
                                 <td>July – August 2026</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>College Opening</td>
                                 <td>Second week of August 2026</td>
                             </tr>
                         </tbody>
                     </table>
                 </div>

                 <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Important Note:</strong> These dates are tentative and based on past academic cycles. Always refer to the official TNEA website (tneaonline.org) for the most accurate and up-to-date information.</p>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">TNEA 2026 Eligibility Criteria</h2>
                 <p>To be eligible for TNEA 2026, candidates must meet specific academic and domicile requirements.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">1. Educational Qualification</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Candidates must have passed Class 12 (10+2) or an equivalent examination from a recognized board. Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics are mandatory subjects.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">2. Minimum Marks Requirement</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         <ul>
                             <li><strong>General Category:</strong> A minimum aggregate of 45% in Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics (PCM).</li>
                             <li><strong>Reserved Categories (SC/ST/OBC):</strong> A minimum aggregate of 40% in PCM.</li>
                         </ul>
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">3. Domicile Requirement</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         <ul>
                             <li>Tamil Nadu native candidates must submit a nativity certificate if they have studied outside the state.</li>
                             <li>Candidates who have studied Class 8 to 12 in Tamil Nadu do not require a nativity certificate.</li>
                             <li>Children of Central Government or PSU employees serving in Tamil Nadu continuously for the past five years are also eligible, subject to producing an employer certificate.</li>
                         </ul>
                     </div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">4. Age Limit</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Generally, there is no upper age limit for TNEA, except for specific courses like Marine Engineering, which may have an age limit of 25 years.</div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">TNEA 2026 Application Process: Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
                 <p>The application for TNEA 2026 is entirely online. Follow these steps to ensure a smooth registration process.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">1. Online Registration</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Visit the official TNEA website (tneaonline.org) and click on the "Application" or "New Registration" link. Provide your name, email ID, and mobile number to register. A unique User ID and password will be generated and sent to your registered contact details.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">2. Login and Fill Personal Details</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Log in using your credentials and fill in your personal, academic, and contact details carefully. This includes educational qualifications, family details, and reservation information if applicable.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">3. Upload Documents</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Upload scanned copies of all required documents, including your photograph, signature, Class 10th and 12th mark sheets, community certificate (if applicable), nativity certificate (if applicable), and other supporting documents as per the specified format and size.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">4. Pay Application Fee</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Pay the non-refundable application fee online using net banking, credit card, debit card, or UPI. The fee is typically ₹500 for the general category and ₹250 for SC/SCA/ST candidates from Tamil Nadu.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">5. Preview and Submit</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">Review all the entered details thoroughly before final submission. Once satisfied, submit the application form. It is advisable to download and print the confirmation page for your records.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">6. Document Verification at TFCs</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">After online registration, candidates will be required to get their certificates verified at designated TNEA Facilitation Centres (TFCs). An online certificate verification process is usually followed, with physical verification for special categories like sports quota.</div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">TNEA 2026 Rank List and Counselling Process</h2>
                 <p>The TNEA rank list is a crucial step, determining your eligibility and priority for seat allotment.</p>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">Rank List Publication</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">The TNEA 2026 rank list will be published online, tentatively in the last week of June 2026. It is prepared based on the marks obtained in Class 12 (Mathematics, Physics, and Chemistry), which are normalized to a total of 200 marks (Mathematics: 100, Physics: 50, Chemistry: 50). A random number is assigned to candidates with the same aggregate marks to resolve ties.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                     <div class="benefit-title">Counselling Procedure</div>
                     <div class="benefit-content">
                         TNEA 2026 counselling will be conducted online in multiple rounds, including general counselling, special reservation counselling, supplementary counselling, and SCA to SC counselling. The key stages include:
                         <ul>
                             <li><strong>Choice Filling:</strong> Candidates select their preferred colleges and engineering courses based on their rank and availability.</li>
                             <li><strong>Tentative Allotment:</strong> Based on choices, rank, and category, a tentative seat is allotted. Candidates must confirm or opt for an upgrade.</li>
                             <li><strong>Provisional Allotment:</strong> Final seat allotment letters are issued after confirmation.</li>
                             <li><strong>Reporting to College:</strong> Candidates must report to their allotted college/TFC with all necessary documents and pay the admission fees within the stipulated time.</li>
                         </ul>
                     </div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title mt-5">Essential Documents for TNEA Counselling 2026</h2>
                 <p>Keep the following documents ready for the application and counselling process:</p>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ Class 10th Mark Sheet</p>
                   <p>✅ Class 12th Mark Sheet/Hall Ticket</p>
                   <p>✅ Transfer Certificate (TC)</p>
                   <p>✅ Community Certificate (if applicable)</p>
                   <p>✅ Nativity Certificate (if applicable, digitally signed e-Certificate preferred)</p>
                   <p>✅ Aadhaar Card or other valid ID proof</p>
                   <p>✅ Passport-size Photographs</p>
                   <p>✅ Parent's Annual Income Details</p>
                   <p>✅ EMIS number</p>
                 </div>

                 <p>The TNEA process is a critical gateway to your engineering aspirations in Tamil Nadu. By staying informed about the tentative dates, understanding the eligibility criteria, and meticulously following the application and counselling steps, you can significantly enhance your chances of securing a seat in a reputed institution. Remember to regularly visit the official TNEA website for all official announcements and updates to ensure a smooth admission journey for TNEA 2026.</p>
             </div>
         </div>
   </div>

            
            
